                        "review": "There is something sortof interesting about this game, but it's just extremely vague. I've put in about 6 hours and just had my first end of a run, but I don't even know why I lost it. I had too much dread, I guess? But dread seems to generate more or less on it's own, and the only way to get rid of it is with contentment, which as far as I know you can only get randomly very occasionally from getting a good sleep. I am probably missing a lot of things here, but why am I still missing all the crucial logic of \"what is this game about?\" and \"what is the loss condition?\" and \"why am I being investigated despite doing nothing but going to my job and giving a passionate speech to not be fired?\". This feels like a game where people have to look up online walkthroughs or something, but as someone who refuses to do that, it's just not fun but instead entirely confusing.",
